From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, uxtheme: reserve padded Aero borders on fixed dialogs

Fixed captioned top-level Aero dialogs need their padded border in the client
geometry as well as in painting. Add the theme's padded border to fixed dialog
layout and AdjustWindowRectEx; use the same width for nonclient hit testing,
system menu geometry, captions, buttons and glass frame rendering. Implement
SM_CXPADDEDBORDER (including its DPI variant), previously returning zero even
when NONCLIENTMETRICS reported four pixels. Fixed borders retain HTBORDER and
do not become resize handles. Basic and ordinary Wine keep their geometry.

Validation: tests/aero-frame.c asserts the 7px side and bottom insets,
AdjustWindowRectEx and HTBORDER, and compares pixels on all four frame sides.
32-bit and 64-bit runs pass; the fixed frame was also verified on screen.
---
diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/window.c b/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 
